// Description: Tests the MLPRO 2 BIO Oblique PCB.test
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
COMMENT: *Example image below*
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: obliquePCB.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set adjustable PSU output 1 to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A and switch the output off.
b. Using TE159, connect the PSU to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
d. Connect the USB cable from the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086) to the PC. 
COMMENT: *Example image below*
DISPLAY: TE192Setup.jpg
CLICK_OK:


#3: Setup equipment 2
a. Using the flat flex ribbon cable connect the Oblique PCB to TE-069 (conn1-conn2).
b. Fit the Test PCB and the Oblique PCB to the ML PRO PCB Fixture 1 (TE190).
c. Using the 20-way ribbon cable connect the TE-069 (PL1) to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192). 
d. Place the TE190 inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
e. Switch the output of the adjustable PSU on and power on the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
DISPLAY: ObliqueSetup1.jpg
COMMENT: Set the address is set to position 2.*Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2

#4: TE-069 PCB communication check

COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM 

Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = BL1,BL2
Returned result is = %BENUM%
IF: %BENUM% STR_EQ BL1,BL2,
GOTO: #4.1

COMMENT: Check the address is set to position 1
PASS_FAIL: #4
GOTO: #5

#4.1: TE-069 PCB communication check - test passed
TEST: PASSED
Result = Test Pass
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat


#5: White LED test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEWHITE 1024
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
PASS_FAIL: #5
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEWHITE 0

#6:IR LED test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEIR 1024
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
PASS_FAIL: #6
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEIR 0

#7: UV LED test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEUV 1024
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
PASS_FAIL: #7
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEUV 0

#8: Test complete:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// turn off any LEDs still on: 

// End of file
